window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["31"]={"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/albania":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"de05ece3ea666de7c2023cea7b8e00625eb680f1e9bd24dd496a81c4581d2497","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/albania","bytes":58396,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Albania travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-01-22T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-10-15T16:44:54+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Demonstrations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Demonstrations have been held in central Tirana, with some reported incidents of violence and property damage."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check local media for the latest information"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay away from any demonstrations, large-scale gatherings or political rallies"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the advice of the local authorities"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/albania/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Albania set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Albanian Embassy in the UK","https://ambasadat.gov.al/united-kingdom/en"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after the day you plan to leave Albania."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual Citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Albania without a visa for up to 90 days in a 180-day period, for tourism or business."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you want to stay longer than 90 days, you must ",["apply in advance for a long-stay visa","https://e-visa.al/apply"]," or ",["apply for a residence permit from within Albania","https://e-albania.al/eAlbaniaServices/UseService.aspx?service_code=15308"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Albania, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Albania guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/2/albania#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Albania. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Albania"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Albania cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate including in places visited by foreigners. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Relations between the majority Muslim population and other ethnic groups in Albania are generally good. The expression of extremist or anti-western views is very rare."]},{"k":"p","s":["Political and other demonstrations have been held in central Tirana, with some reported incidents of violence. Demonstrations can cause traffic diversions and other disruption. Demonstrations could happen elsewhere, and may take place outside the capital city."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check local media for the latest information"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid any demonstrations, large-scale gatherings or political rallies"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the advice of the local authorities"]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is crime and violence in some areas, but reports of crime targeting foreigners are rare. There have been occasional shootings and small explosions related to internal disputes over criminal, business or political interests."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take sensible precautions to protect yourself from street crime, particularly in larger cities and late at night."]},{"k":"p","s":["Watch out for pickpockets and bag thieves in tourist areas, on buses and trains and major public transport hubs, including airports."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Penalties for drug-related crimes are severe."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Possession of illegal drugs could result in a prison sentence of 5 to 10 years. The penalty for supplying drugs is up to 15 years in prison."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Albania have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items, including cannabis. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Being arrested"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Albanian authorities do not always inform the British Embassy when British nationals have been arrested. If you are detained, you may insist on your right to contact the ",["British Embassy in Tirana","https://www.gov.uk/world/organisations/british-embassy-tirana"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex relationships are legal in Albania. Anti-discrimination and anti-hate-crime legislation is in place. Tirana has several gay-friendly bars and a number of LGBT+ support groups."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Water sports and swimming safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are some local press reports that jet skis and boats being rented along the coasts may lack adequate safety precautions and equipment."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are considering taking part in water sports activities, do so through a licensed water sports centre and make sure paperwork is completed before starting the activity."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["watersports safety abroad","https://www.rospa.com/leisure-water-safety/water/advice/watersports-abroad"]," from the Royal Society for the Prevention of Accidents."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take note of warning signs, follow instructions from lifeguards and observe the flag indicators on beaches. Take local advice if jellyfish or urchins are present."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["2023 European Environment Agency report","https://www.eea.europa.eu/en/countries/cooperating-countries/albania"]," noted that a small number of beaches are polluted because of inadequate sewage disposal and treatment."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Albania, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in the RAC’s Albania guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/albania/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may find it useful to have a ",["1968 international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well as your UK licence. The 1949 IDP is not accepted any more. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must carry a ",["green card","https://www.gov.uk/vehicle-insurance/driving-abroad"]," as proof of vehicle insurance to drive your car in Albania. If you’re planning to hire a car, check with your car hire company for information on their requirements before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check if you need a ",["UK sticker to drive your car outside the UK","https://www.gov.uk/displaying-number-plates/flags-identifiers-and-stickers"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you stay longer than one year, or live in Albania, you will need to apply for an Albanian driving licence."]},{"k":"p","s":["To import a vehicle into Albania, make sure you have all the necessary papers on arrival at the border. Consult the Albanian Embassy in the UK before you leave. The British Embassy will be unable to help anyone attempting to bring a vehicle into Albania without the correct paperwork."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dangers of driving in Albania"]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving can be very hazardous and often aggressive and erratic. Deaths from road traffic accidents are amongst the highest in Europe. Police have taken some measures to decrease the number of accidents."]},{"k":"p","s":["Minor traffic disputes can quickly escalate, especially as some motorists could be armed. Avoid reacting to provocative behaviour by other road users."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are involved in a traffic accident, even a minor one, remain at the scene until the police arrive. This will usually happen quite quickly in built-up areas. Failing to wait could result in charges under the Albanian Penal Code and you could get a fine."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Road surfaces are poor, especially in rural areas. If you are travelling at night, watch out for unmarked roadworks, potholes and vehicles without lights. Four-wheel drive vehicles are more practical on rural and minor roads."]},{"k":"p","s":["Power cuts can affect street lighting in towns and cities. Elsewhere, even on the major routes, there is no street lighting."]},{"k":"h","s":["Landmines"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are still unexploded landmines in some remote areas around hill towns on the northern border with Kosovo. Take care, particularly if hiking, and follow any warning signs. Do not walk on uncultivated land or step off the marked paths. If in doubt, seek local advice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of earthquakes – tremors are common. Serious earthquakes are less frequent but do happen."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding and snow"]},{"k":"p","s":["From December to February, severe weather may cause flooding, particularly in northern Albania. Heavy snowfall in mountainous areas can lead to disruption to transport and services. Monitor local and international media for the latest information."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildfires"]},{"k":"p","s":["Wildfires are common in Albania from April to October due to the dry and hot weather. Wildfires are highly dangerous and unpredictable. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["take care when visiting or driving through countryside"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure cigarette ends are properly extinguished"]},{"k":"li","s":["not light fires or barbecues except in designated and marked areas"]},{"k":"li","s":["not leave any rubbish"]},{"k":"p","s":["Causing a wildfire or a forest fire is a criminal offence in Albania. Penalties could result from fines to imprisonment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be cautious if you are in or near an area affected by wildfires. During the event of a wildfire, you should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["call the emergency services on 112"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow any advice from the local emergency services"]},{"k":"li","s":["contact your airline or travel operator who can assist you with return travel to the UK"]},{"k":"li","s":["if you need consular assistance call +355 4 223 4973/4/5 during ",["working hours","https://www.gov.uk/world/organisations/british-embassy-tirana/office/british-embassy"]," or +44 207 008 5000 out of hours"]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 127 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Albania","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/2/albania#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face Albania","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/2/albania"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Albania. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air pollution"]},{"k":"p","s":["There can be high levels of air pollution in Albania. You can find further information and advice on air quality on the ",["World Health Organization (WHO)","https://www.who.int/airpollution/en/"]," website and check air quality levels on the ",["World Air Quality Index website","https://aqicn.org/map/europe/"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tap water and milk"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not drink the tap water in Albania, as it may cause illness. Only drink bottled water. If you drink milk, make sure it is UHT (ultra high temperature) or pasteurised milk."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Albania"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical and dental facilities, including accident and emergency facilities, are very poor, particularly outside Tirana. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad, evacuation by air ambulance and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["list of medical providers in Albania","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/albania-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Albania"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 127"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 128"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 112"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Albania"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Albania"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Albania"]," in Albania"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Albania","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/albania-bereavement-guide"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Albania","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/albania-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/albania/british-embassy-tirana"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/albania/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":14071,"change":"New information about demonstrations in Tirana ('Warnings and insurance' page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/colombia":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"4b640d43b55f31472793d3f79202161b81d177330a71101d0a007b89c6d1a5ae","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/colombia","bytes":95374,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Colombia travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-21T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-10-30T00:40:46+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Temporary deployment of security forces in the city of Cucuta"]},{"k":"p","s":["On 29 October, President de la Espriella ordered the temporary deployment of security forces in the city of Cucuta. Further security measures are expected in the coming days. Travellers should plan ahead, follow advice of local authorities, and see the ‘Safety and security’ pages."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against all but essential travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Colombia-Venezuela border and northern Colombia"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["all of Norte de Santander Department, including Cúcuta."]},{"k":"li","s":["all of Arauca Department"]},{"k":"li","s":["the municipality of Puerto Carreño in Vichada Department"]},{"k":"li","s":["within 5km of the rest of the border with Venezuela."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO currently advises against all travel to ",["Venezuela’s border regions with Colombia","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/venezuela"],". You should not use any of the Colombia-Venezuela land crossings."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Pacific coast and Colombia-Panama border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Chocó Department, except for the department capital Quibdó, the towns of Nuquí and Bahía Solano and Capurganá"]},{"k":"li","s":["the western part of Valle del Cauca Department, including Buenaventura"]},{"k":"li","s":["the municipality of Jamundí, Valle del Cauca"]},{"k":"li","s":["the South Pacific, Sanquianga and Telembi regions of Nariño Department"]},{"k":"li","s":["the southern part of Córdoba Department"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Urabá and Bajo Cauca regions of Antioquia Department"]},{"k":"li","s":["the southern part of Bolívar Department"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Central Colombia"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["all of Guaviare Department, except for the department capital San José del Guaviare"]},{"k":"li","s":["Cartagena del Chairá, San Vicente del Caguan, Puerto Rico, El Doncello, Paujil and La Montañita in Caquetá Department"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Ariari region of southern Meta, except for Caño Cristales"]},{"k":"p","s":["If travelling to the tourist site of Caño Cristales, travel by air from the town of La Macarena with a reputable tour company."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Colombia-Ecuador border and southern Colombia"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to within 5km of the border with Ecuador except for:"]},{"k":"li","s":["all of Cauca Department, except for the department capital Popayán"]},{"k":"li","s":["the border crossing on the Pan-American highway at the Puente Internacional de Rumichaca"]},{"k":"li","s":["the city of Ipiales in Nariño Department"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to Orito, San Miguel, Valle del Guamuez, Puerto Caicedo, Puerto Guzmán, Puerto Asis and Puerto Leguizamo in Putumayo Department."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/colombia/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. If you have onward travel plans within the region, check travel advice for all destinations you plan to travel through. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://webarchive.nationalarchives.gov.uk/ukgwa/20260804150650mp_/https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://webarchive.nationalarchives.gov.uk/ukgwa/20260804150650mp_/https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://webarchive.nationalarchives.gov.uk/ukgwa/20260804150650mp_/https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://webarchive.nationalarchives.gov.uk/ukgwa/20260804150650mp_/https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://webarchive.nationalarchives.gov.uk/ukgwa/20260804150650mp_/https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://webarchive.nationalarchives.gov.uk/ukgwa/20260804150650mp_/https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://webarchive.nationalarchives.gov.uk/ukgwa/20260804150650mp_/https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://webarchive.nationalarchives.gov.uk/ukgwa/20260804150650mp_/https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/colombia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://webarchive.nationalarchives.gov.uk/ukgwa/20260804150650mp_/https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://webarchive.nationalarchives.gov.uk/ukgwa/20260804150650mp_/https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://webarchive.nationalarchives.gov.uk/ukgwa/20260804150650mp_/https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Colombia’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Colombia set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Colombian Embassy in the UK","https://reinounido.embajada.gov.co/"]," (for English choose ‘Ingles’ from the drop down menu)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Colombia, your passport must be valid on entry. However, Colombian immigration authorities recommend your passport has an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you plan to leave."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["British-Colombian dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a British-Colombian dual national, you must enter and leave Colombia using your Colombian passport and Colombian identification card (Cedula)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Colombia for up to 90 days without a visa for business or tourism, at the discretion of the Colombian immigration officer on arrival."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must be able to show an onward or return ticket valid within the 90-day period."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check the latest entry requirements and how to apply for a visa with the ",["Colombian Consulate General","https://londres.consulado.gov.co/"]," in London before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have a Colombian visa with more than 90 days of validity, you must register the visa at a ",["Migración Colombia office","https://unidad-administrativa-especial-migracion-colombia.micolombiadigital.gov.co/cedula-de-extranjeria/agende-su-cita"]," (in Spanish) or ",["register the visa online","https://apps.migracioncolombia.gov.co/registro/public/formularioRegistro.jsf"]," (in Spanish) within 15 days of arrival in Colombia. If you do not register, you may get a fine."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may be able to extend your stay once you are in Colombia by up to 120 days by applying at the immigration office ",["Migración Colombia","https://unidad-administrativa-especial-migracion-colombia.micolombiadigital.gov.co/directorio-institucional/unidad-administrativa-especial-migracion-colombia"]," (in Spanish). As a visitor, you cannot remain in Colombia for more than 180 days in any 12-month period."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you overstay your visa, you could get a fine, or be deported at your own cost."]},{"k":"h","s":["Checks at border control"]},{"k":"p","s":["Colombian authorities advise that you can speed up your entry to the country by ",["completing the ‘Check-Mig’ form on Migración Colombia","https://apps.migracioncolombia.gov.co/pre-registro/en/DatosViaje"],", although this is not mandatory. You can complete the form between 72 hours and one hour before you travel to Colombia. You will receive a confirmation email that you will need to show to immigration officials when you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you get your passport stamped."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter Colombia by land, sea or river, make sure the immigration authorities stamp your passport. If it is not stamped, you could get a fine when you leave. If the immigration office on the border is closed, go to the nearest office of ",["Migración Colombia","https://unidad-administrativa-especial-migracion-colombia.micolombiadigital.gov.co/directorio-institucional/unidad-administrativa-especial-migracion-colombia"]," (in Spanish)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling with children"]},{"k":"p","s":["Children aged 17 and under who have resident status in Colombia and who are travelling on a British passport need a ",["notarised letter of permission from any non-accompanying parents or parent","https://www.migracioncolombia.gov.co/entidad/salida-de-menores-del-pais"]," (in Spanish). The letter must be authenticated by a notary or by a Colombian consulate. You can get more information from Migración Colombia (in Spanish) or by contacting the ",["Colombian Consulate in the UK","https://londres.consulado.gov.co/"]," (in Spanish)."]},{"k":"h","s":["San Andres Archipelago"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling to the islands of San Andres, Providencia or Santa Catalina, you must buy a tourist card from the boarding gate, on the day of the flight. You do not need one if you’re staying less than 24 hours."]},{"k":"h","s":["Departure tax"]},{"k":"p","s":["Departure tax is usually included in the price of the airline ticket, but check with your airline."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Colombia, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you are arriving from certain countries with a transmission risk. You may also be asked to show it if you are travelling to areas in Colombia which are considered high risk. Carry your vaccination certificate at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Colombia guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/53/colombia#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Colombia","https://www.dian.gov.co/"]," (in Spanish). You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Colombia"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can bring up to 10,000 US dollars-worth of any currency into Colombia. You must declare anything above this amount with the ",["National Tax and Customs Directorate (DIAN)","https://www.dian.gov.co/Viajeros-y-Servicios-aduaneros/Paginas/Inicio.aspx"]," (in Spanish)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Colombia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are very likely to try to carry out attacks in Colombia."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Armed groups"]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite the landmark peace agreement between the government and the Revolutionary Armed Forces of Colombia (FARC) in 2016, many armed groups remain active throughout the country."]},{"k":"p","s":["These groups may attack with little or no warning. The focus is predominantly in areas where there are active illicit economies and narco-trafficking but attacks have historically targeted some tourist locations, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["transportation hubs including airports"]},{"k":"li","s":["markets and shopping malls"]},{"k":"li","s":["local government facilities"]},{"k":"li","s":["hotels, clubs and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["places of worship"]},{"k":"li","s":["parks and other public areas"]},{"k":"li","s":["major sporting and cultural events"]},{"k":"li","s":["educational institutions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police and military personnel and installations are frequently targeted, including in large cities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Past methods of attack have included car bombs, grenade and drone attacks, and explosive devices left in buildings and on main roads. Stay alert and follow the advice of the local security authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Regularly reassess your security arrangements and consider carefully any travel around the country."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Colombia has suffered from internal armed conflict for over 50 years. In 2016, Colombia’s then-President Juan Manuel Santos signed a peace agreement with the Revolutionary Armed Forces of Colombia (FARC) movement to end the civil war."]},{"k":"p","s":["The peace agreement is still in place today, but Colombia remains seriously affected by conflict. Delays in the implementation of the peace agreement have led to a resurgence in violence in parts of the country. Much of this involves armed groups fighting for control of territory, the cocaine trade, and other illicit economies."]},{"k":"h","s":["Protests"]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests and demonstrations happen regularly throughout the country and often start at short notice. They can turn violent and may lead to an increase in the police and military presence. Road closures and roadblocks can cause travel disruptions for visitors."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid protests, strikes and demonstrations and follow the advice of local authorities or tour operators if you are affected. Allow extra time to reach your destination and monitor local media, including social media channels."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a heightened risk of violence across the country when elections are held due to the interference of armed groups and criminal gangs in the electoral process. During national and state elections, avoid large gatherings or political rallies and be alert around polling stations."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Drugs, organised crime and terrorism are inextricably linked in Colombia. There’s evidence of high levels of coca cultivation in:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Nariño Department"]},{"k":"li","s":["Cauca Department"]},{"k":"li","s":["Putumayo Department"]},{"k":"li","s":["Caquetá Department"]},{"k":"li","s":["Meta Department"]},{"k":"li","s":["Guaviare Department"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Catatumbo region in Norte de Santander Department"]},{"k":"li","s":["northern Antioquia Department"]},{"k":"li","s":["southern Bolivar Department"]},{"k":"p","s":["There’s a risk to your safety in any area where coca, marijuana or opium poppies are cultivated and near to cocaine processing labs."]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal armed groups and criminal gangs are active in all of the departments where coca is cultivated, processed or transported, as well as in many cities. The risk is particularly significant in:"]},{"k":"li","s":["rural areas near to the borders with Panama, Venezuela and Ecuador"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Parque Nacional Natural de La Macarena in the Department of Meta"]},{"k":"li","s":["the port towns of Buenaventura in the Department of Valle de Cauca, Turbo in the Department of Antioquia and Tumaco in the Department of Nariño"]},{"k":"p","s":["Money laundering, extortion and prostitution rackets are all part of organised crime activity."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Street crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pickpocketing, mugging and armed robbery are a problem, especially in major cities, including Bogotá, Medellín, Cali and the Caribbean coast. British nationals have been robbed at gunpoint in the Candelaria area of Bogotá and across many cities in Colombia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be vigilant in public places used by foreign nationals or near official buildings. Take care on city streets, especially in deprived areas of cities, after dark or if you are on your own. Do not carry large amounts of money or wear expensive-looking jewellery or watches."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Criminal kidnapping"]},{"k":"p","s":["Short-term opportunistic abductions known as ‘express kidnappings’ are common in Colombia. Criminals – often posing as taxi drivers may track and select a target victim, often from around ATMs and often at night. They also attack at random. The kidnappers force the victim to empty their bank account by making multiple transfers, or drive them to ATMs and force them to withdraw cash. Normally victims are quickly released, but there have been incidents where those who have resisted the kidnappers’ demands have been killed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be aware of your surroundings and always let someone you trust know your whereabouts. Use ATMs during business hours so you can go inside a bank, supermarket or shopping centre."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you fall victim to a kidnapping, follow the kidnapper’s instructions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kidnapping rates remain high and widespread in Colombia. Illegal armed groups kidnap hostages – both for ransom and for political purposes. While foreign nationals are not the primary targets, foreigners have been kidnapped in recent years, particularly those working for (or believed to be working for) oil, mining and related companies where armed groups operate."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals are seen as legitimate targets, including tourists, humanitarian aid workers, journalists and business travellers. If you are kidnapped, the reason for your presence is unlikely to protect you or secure your safe release."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drug assisted robberies and sexual assaults"]},{"k":"p","s":["The British Embassy has received reports of criminals in Colombia using drugs to subdue their victims. This includes the use of scopolamine, which temporarily incapacitates victims. Criminals can administer drugs through food, drinks, cigarettes, aerosols and even paper flyers. Victims become disoriented quickly and are vulnerable to robbery, sexual assault, rape and other crimes."]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals use dating applications and websites to identify and lure foreign nationals who are travelling alone and looking to meet local people. Criminals work in teams, with women easing the victim into a false sense of security. Victims are incapacitated and robbed. Incidents have been reported in nightclubs, bars, restaurants, public transportation, including taxis, and on city streets. Do not accept invitations from strangers to their accommodation, and do not invite strangers to your accommodation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not leave food or drinks unattended and do not take anything offered by strangers. These drugs can cause serious medical problems, including loss of consciousness, memory loss and can be fatal if administered in large quantities. Get local medical attention as soon as possible."]},{"k":"p","s":["Where possible, plan how you will travel to and from your destination. Only use pre-booked taxis."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public offences"]},{"k":"p","s":["The law against the sexual abuse of children (aged 13 and under) is strictly enforced, especially when it involves tourists. If convicted, you could face a long prison sentence."]},{"k":"p","s":["The 141 national toll-free line and the ",["Child and Adolescent Police","https://www.policia.gov.co/proteccion-infancia"]," are available for 24-hour protection, emergencies and orientation of children and young people."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Police scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals posing as police are known to operate in Bogotá and elsewhere. They may ask to inspect money to see if it is counterfeit. If you are approached, ask them to escort you to the nearest local police station (CAI or ‘Centro de Atención Inmediata’)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Crime in rural areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["In many rural areas, the authority of the Colombian state is limited, and the British Embassy’s ability to help British nationals in trouble in these areas will also be limited. Mobile and internet connection in rural areas is often limited."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry a colour printout of the photo page and Colombian visa from your passport for identification. Keep the passport somewhere safe."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to consume alcohol in public spaces."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Colombia has severe penalties for possession, use or trafficking of illegal drugs."]},{"k":"p","s":["Colombian drug detection methods are sophisticated and anyone attempting to traffic drugs can expect to be arrested. British nationals have been arrested and detained for trying to smuggle cocaine out of the country. Prison conditions are harsh. Pack your own luggage and keep it with you at all times. Lock your cases to protect them from tampering. Never carry items for other people. Never exchange money for strangers, as this is a common practice among money launderers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Spiritual cleansing"]},{"k":"p","s":["Traditional hallucinogenic tea, known as Yagé or Ayahuasca, is brewed and marketed to tourists as spiritual cleansing. The various preparations typically contain dimethyltryptamine (DMT), a strong hallucinogen that’s illegal in the UK and many other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are many risks involved. Consumption is not regulated. Intoxicated travellers have been assaulted and robbed. There have also been reports of sexual assaults during these ceremonies."]},{"k":"p","s":["Health risks are not well understood and some people have suffered serious illnesses and in some cases death after taking these drugs. The jungle retreats are often a long way from medical facilities making the risks even greater. Some have basic medical services, but others do not. Some do not have an established plan for how you can access medical facilities in case of an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking photos in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Photographing military or strategic government sites is illegal."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is legal in Colombia, but same-sex relationships are not widely accepted, especially in rural areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can exchange US dollars and euros at banks and authorised money exchanges. Do not change money on the street."]},{"k":"p","s":["Credit and debit cards are widely accepted in hotels, shops and restaurants. Keep the receipts in case you need to show customs what money you have spent when you leave."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive a hire car or a UK vehicle, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Colombia. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["a year of driving experience"]},{"k":"li","s":["being aged 18 years and over"]},{"k":"li","s":["holding an International Driving Permit (IDP)"]},{"k":"li","s":["a citizenship card or passport"]},{"k":"li","s":["a credit card to guarantee the vehicle hire"]},{"k":"p","s":["Carry all vehicle documents in physical form, in case you are pulled over by the police."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving standards"]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards are poor and traffic accidents are common. Avoid driving at night, which can be particularly hazardous. Do not hitch-hike. The risk of violence and kidnapping is higher in some rural areas, and there is a risk of being robbed at roadblocks set up by illegal armed groups. Main roads are generally safe during daylight hours."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public transport"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be cautious when using public transport in Colombia."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been several recent incidents of armed robbery on buses. Avoid displaying valuable items like laptops, cameras and mobile phones. Do not wear jewellery and only carry minimal amounts of cash. Avoid travelling on your own or at night, especially at border crossings or areas where there are few other people around. When travelling to remote areas, it may be safer to travel with others or take part in a tour with a reputable company."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been reports of express kidnappings, assaults and robberies in unlicensed taxis. Use licensed telephone or internet-based taxi services whenever possible or book through your hotel. Many restaurants in Colombia will book a taxi for you. Do not hail taxis on the street."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are authorised taxi booths at most airports in Colombia. Bogotá’s El Dorado International Airport only allows authorised taxis to pick up passengers at its terminals. Authorised taxis are yellow with white licence plates and plate numbers on doors and roof. The driver’s information will be shown inside the vehicle. Well-known taxi companies can be booked via Uber and Cabify."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Landmines"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk from landmines throughout Colombia, especially in rural and remote areas. Mined areas are often unmarked. Be vigilant when visiting remote areas or travelling off the main roads."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["The departmental capitals of Amazonas, Vaupes and Guainía are only accessible by air due to the lack of road infrastructure in these departments."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["2026-2027 El Niño"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Colombian Government has officially declared an El Niño phenomenon, with a high probability of a strong to very strong intensity until at least March 2027."]},{"k":"p","s":["El Niño is expected to generate unusually heavy rainfall, possible flooding and landslides, as well as higher temperatures, drought and wildfires. These may disrupt travel and other services."]},{"k":"p","s":["Extreme weather may affect your travel plans. Monitor local news and weather reports and follow the advice of local authorities. For official updates and forecasts, visit the ",["Colombian government website","https://www.ideam.gov.co/fenomeno-del-nino"]," (in Spanish)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hurricanes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although uncommon, hurricanes and tropical storms can affect the Caribbean coast and the Archipelago of San Andres, Providencia and Santa Catalina."]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor local news and check ",["World Meteorological Organization weather reports for Colombia","https://worldweather.wmo.int/en/country.html?countryCode=COL"],", the ",["US National Hurricane Center","https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/"],", and the Institute of Hydrology, Meteorology and Environmental Studies (IDEAM) (in Spanish)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high risk of earthquakes across Colombia. Earthquakes occur regularly, particularly in Santander Department and the Andean Region."]},{"k":"p","s":["Familiarise yourself with safety procedures and any instructions in your hotel or accommodation."]},{"k":"p","s":["If an earthquake happens, monitor local media reports, follow instructions from the authorities and keep essential belongings, such as your passport and money, with you."]},{"k":"p","s":["Get real-time information (in Spanish) following an earthquake from:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["National Unit for Disaster Risk Management (UNGRD)","https://portal.gestiondelriesgo.gov.co/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Colombia’s Geological Services","https://www.sgc.gov.co/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["You can find a real-time earthquake map and further information about earthquakes in Colombia from ",["Colombia’s Geological Services","https://www.sgc.gov.co/sismos"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of floods and landslides after heavy rains throughout Colombia, especially in the Colombian Andes. Get local advice before travelling on mountain roads after heavy rain."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Volcanic eruptions"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are 25 active and monitored volcanoes in Colombia. Check the latest ",["daily bulletins about volcanic activity","https://www2.sgc.gov.co/Noticias/boletinesDocumentos/Forms/AllItems.aspx"]," (in Spanish)."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are in areas of volcanic activity, monitor the ",["Servicio Geológico Colombiano","https://www.sgc.gov.co/volcanes"]," for any updates or alerts."]},{"k":"p","s":["Notify friends and family of your location, stay alert, and follow any advice from local security authorities or your travel operator. Be prepared to make travel arrangements or follow evacuation plans at short notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check before travelling on the Pan-American highway, which passes near a volcano. Call 767 for information (in Spanish) from the Colombian Highway Police about road closures."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Colombia. It only covers regions where the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/colombia"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/colombia/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Colombia-Venezuela border and northern Colombia"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Catatumbo region of Norte de Santander Department"]},{"k":"li","s":["all of Arauca Department, except for the department capital, Arauca"]},{"k":"li","s":["the municipality of Puerto Carreño in Vichada Department, except for the department capital, Puerto Carreño"]},{"k":"li","s":["within 5km of the rest of the border with Venezuela, except for the city of Cúcuta"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO currently advises against all travel to ",["Venezuela’s border regions with Colombia","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/venezuela"],". You should not use any of the Colombia-Venezuela land crossings."]},{"k":"h","s":["Pacific coast and Colombia-Panama border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Chocó Department, except for the department capital Quibdó, the whale-watching towns of Nuquí and Bahía Solano and the tourist site of Capurganá"]},{"k":"li","s":["the western part of Valle del Cauca Department, including Buenaventura"]},{"k":"li","s":["the municipality of Jamundí, Valle del Cauca"]},{"k":"li","s":["the western part of Cauca Department"]},{"k":"li","s":["the South Pacific, Sanquianga and Telembi regions of Nariño Department"]},{"k":"li","s":["the southern part of Córdoba Department"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Urabá and Bajo Cauca regions of Antioquia Department"]},{"k":"li","s":["the southern part of Bolívar Department"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Pacific coast of Chocó is a popular eco-tourist destination. However, much of Chocó is remote. Illegal armed groups are active and involved in the drugs trade throughout the department and particularly near the border with Panama. If you intend to travel to the whale-watching towns of Bahia Solano and Nuqui, only do so by air and do not travel inland or along the coast out of town."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Darien Gap"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ‘Darien Gap’ is a dangerous area renowned for the presence of several illegal armed groups, illegal migration and drugs trafficking. There’s no road crossing between Colombia and Panama. Avoid crossing between Panama and Colombia by land."]},{"k":"h","s":["Colombia-Ecuador border and southern Colombia"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to within 5km of the border with Ecuador except for:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the border crossing on the Pan-American highway at the Puente Internacional de Rumichaca"]},{"k":"li","s":["the city of Ipiales in Nariño Department"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to Orito, San Miguel, Valle del Guamuez, Puerto Caicedo, Puerto Guzmán, Puerto Asis and Puerto Leguizamo in Putumayo Department."]},{"k":"h","s":["Central Colombia"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["all of Guaviare Department, except for the department capital San José de Guaviare"]},{"k":"li","s":["Cartagena del Chairá, San Vicente del Caguan, Puerto Rico, El Doncello, Paujil and La Montañita in Caquetá Department"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Ariari region of southern Meta, except for Caño Cristales"]},{"k":"p","s":["If travelling to the tourist site of Caño Cristales, travel by air from the town of La Macarena with a reputable tour company."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ciudad Perdida – ‘Lost City’"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you travel to the ‘Lost City’ in the Sierra Nevada de Santa Marta, only do so as part of an organised tour."]},{"k":"h","s":["San Agustín Archaeological Park"]},{"k":"p","s":["The San Agustín Archaeological Park (‘Parque Arqueológico de San Agustín’) is in the department of Huila. Enter and leave the park on the main road through Neiva or Popayán."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 123 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Colombia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/53/colombia#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Colombia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/53/colombia"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Yellow fever"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika"]},{"k":"li","s":["Malaria"]},{"k":"li","s":["Dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["Chikungunya"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Colombia, including Bogotá and areas in the Departments of Cundinamarca, Boyacá, Nariño and Antioquia. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drinking tap water"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tap water is safe to drink only in Bogotá. You should drink only bottled water and avoid ice in drinks."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication and prescriptions"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can find most medication in pharmacies in large cities, but medicine for complex treatment may be unavailable in rural areas and small towns. You may need a prescription from a local doctor to get some controlled medicine."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you take prescription medication, you will be responsible for determining its legality in Colombia. Always keep your medication in the original container, bring sufficient quantities of your medication with you, pack your medication in your carry-on luggage and carry a copy of your prescriptions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pharmacies in Colombia (‘droguerías’) have a cross on their signage and are easy to find in the main cities in Colombia. They are less common in rural areas. Most pharmacies in Colombia will have a delivery service. Prescriptions must be written in Spanish, in the metric system and using the medicine’s generic name."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Colombia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities in Colombia vary widely in quality. In large cities and state capitals, private clinics provide good quality care for routine and complex treatment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Public health facilities and those in smaller cities are generally ill equipped and poorly funded. Ambulance services in remote areas are unreliable and public hospitals often lack adequate medical supplies."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Colombia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/colombia-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Colombia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 123"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 119"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 123"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=colombia"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=colombia"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=colombia"]," in Colombia"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Colombia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/colombia-bereavement-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Colombia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/colombia-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"]," such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/colombia/british-embassy-bogota"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/colombia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Colombia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-colombia"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":31732,"change":"New information about the the temporary deployment of security forces in the city of Cucuta (‘Warnings and Insurance’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/what-scotland-is-getting-wrong-on-recycling-and-wales-is-getting-right-295633":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"276a29163b43d58921b76cf232bf853c9fa9b0214df54fb2fe94298bd72d2d24","read":"https://theconversation.com/what-scotland-is-getting-wrong-on-recycling-and-wales-is-getting-right-295633","bytes":181141,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"What Scotland is getting wrong on recycling – and Wales is getting right","by":[{"n":"Ian Williams","r":"Professor of Applied Environmental Science, University of Southampton"}],"pub":"2026-11-16T10:11:20Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Scotland has ambitions to become an environmental leader, but its recycling rate has just fallen to a five-year low."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Scottish household ",["recycling","https://theconversation.com/uk/search?q=recycling"]," rate fell from 44.3% in 2024 to 42.8% in 2025, according to ",["recently released figures","https://www.circularonline.co.uk/news/scottish-household-recycling-rate-falls-to-42-8-as-incineration-rises/"],". These ",["figures","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c62ke84qwl1vo"]," also show the levels vary widely across the country, with Glasgow one of the lowest local authorities at only 24% and Clackmannanshire at 56%. The Scottish government had previously set a ",["recycling target","https://www.environment.gov.scot/our-environment/people-and-the-environment/waste-and-resources"]," of 70% of waste by 2025."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is tempting to blame Scottish households. But research has shown recycling is shaped by social, cultural and structural conditions. ",["Participation improves","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resconrec.2005.09.005"]," when services fit people’s everyday lives and make recycling convenient. People need authorities to provide suitable local infrastructure, services and behavioural support to enable ",["effective recycling","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.wasman.2010.12.010"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Scotland’s recycling services remain ",["inconsistent and confusing","https://www.gov.scot/publications/household-recycling-code-practice-consultation-document/"],". This is partly down to the continuing variation between local authority systems. Depending on where someone lives, there can be differences in which materials are accepted, container types and colours and whether glass is collected at the kerbside."]},{"k":"p","s":["The wide variation between councils, from 18.2% to 56.5%, ",["points to inconsistent services","https://www.gov.scot/publications/household-recycling-code-practice-consultation-document/"]," rather than individual attitudes alone."]},{"k":"p","s":["Meanwhile, Scotland has struggled to introduce a ",["return scheme","https://www.gov.scot/publications/deposit-return-scheme-scotland-regulations-2020-amended-deposit-return-scheme-scotland-amendment-regulations-2025-deposit-return-scheme-scotland-designation-scheme-administrator-order-2025-full-bria/pages/7/"]," for drinks containers, where a deposit is paid and then returned when recycled. Initially expected to start in October 2025, this has been postponed to October 2027, and will no longer include glass, due to wrangles with ",["the UK government","https://consoc.org.uk/the-deposit-return-scheme/"]," over devolved powers."]},{"k":"p","s":["This was expected to raise recycling levels of eligible drinks containers to ",["around 90%","https://www.zerowastescotland.org.uk/resources/deposit-return-scheme-environmental-benefits"],". A similar ",["deposit scheme","https://re-turn.ie/2-5-billion-cans-and-bottles-re-turned/"]," in Ireland has been very successful at pushing up recycling levels."]},{"k":"h","s":["What Wales gets right"]},{"k":"p","s":[["UK-wide figures","https://www.gov.uk/government/statistics/uk-waste-data/uk-statistics-on-waste"]," also show a distinct difference between the four nations: Wales recycled 58.6% (up from 4.8% of household waste in ",["1998-99","https://www.gov.wales/new-stats-why-wales-outlier-uk-recycling-rates"],"), Northern Ireland 50.1%, England 43.8% and Scotland comes bottom at 42.7% in 2024. These outcomes reflect political choices, not simply how diligently households sort their rubbish. Scotland’s lower rate reflects ",["lack of access","https://www.gov.scot/publications/waste-reprocessing-infrastructure-scotland/"]," to convenient collection systems, cost barriers, limited reprocessing capacity and increasing incineration of recyclables."]},{"k":"p","s":["Overall, recycling has stalled across England, Scotland and Northern Ireland while ",["incineration of waste has expanded","https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5eabdfbe067c0b62fc7b58b7/t/6800cd36c2408b1f7ad8f645/1744883006223/uk-energy-from-waste-statistics-2024-4812.pdf"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The municipal rate of recycling has ",["increased to 68.4% in 2024-25","https://www.gov.wales/local-authority-municipal-waste-management-april-2024-march-2025-html"],". Municipal waste includes all local-authority-collected waste, including some commercial waste, street sweepings and litter bins."]},{"k":"p","s":["But ",["Wales shows","https://www.mdpi.com/2313-4321/7/4/46"]," that stagnation in recycling levels is not inevitable, and the nation has become a ",["global leader","https://www.gov.wales/new-stats-why-wales-outlier-uk-recycling-rates"]," on this front."]},{"k":"p","s":["This reflects a sustained Welsh government policy, ",["reinforced in 2021 with a new approach","https://www.gov.wales/beyond-recycling"]," that set statutory local authority targets, invested in collections, as well as monitoring and political backing. Wales also imposed a moratorium on new large-scale ",["energy-from-waste developments in 2021","https://www.mrw.co.uk/news/wales-introduces-immediate-moratorium-on-efw-24-03-2021/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Welsh system is not perfect. Its municipal rate remained below the 70% national target for 2024-25. Nevertheless, ",["20 of its 22 local authorities improved","https://www.gov.wales/local-authority-municipal-waste-management-april-2024-march-2025-html"],", demonstrating what sustained institutional pressure can achieve. Its experience suggests that targets work best when they are backed by infrastructure, accountability and stable long-term policy."]},{"k":"h","s":["Recycling history"]},{"k":"p","s":["The first UK recycling in the early 2000s focused on relatively accessible materials such as paper, glass, metals and ",["garden waste","https://doi.org/10.1016/S0921-3449(02)00106-4"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["But further progress depends on addressing ",["food waste","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.wasman.2026.115536"],", ",["plastic films","https://www.mdpi.com/2073-4360/18/16/2031"],", ",["textiles","https://www.mdpi.com/2673-7248/5/4/41"],", ",["electrical products","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.wasman.2020.10.016"]," and ",["complex packaging","https://doi.org/10.3390/su17020556"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["These streams are harder to collect, separate and process, while markets for some recovered materials, where waste is reused, remain uncertain. Variable quality, volatile prices and weak demand for some materials increase costs and risk, potentially ",["leaving councils without buyers","https://democracy.swansea.gov.uk/documents/s110653/9%20-%20Scrutiny%20-%20Recyclate%20Income%20Report%20Final.pdf?"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Another reason recycling have not climbed as high as predicted is that people cannot recycle materials that councils do not collect. To help people recycle more it is important to ",["eliminate confusing labels","https://product.sustainability-directory.com/question/why-are-some-plastic-recycling-labels-confusing/"],", redesign packaging that was ",["never designed to be recycled","https://www.asa.org.uk/news/disposing-of-misleading-ads.html"]," or create new markets for recovered materials."]},{"k":"h","s":["Burning not burying"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s important to note that landfill reduction is also an important environmental achievement, and in Scotland, for instance, landfill use has declined – ",["down 82.5% since 2011","https://shiny.data.gov.scot/sepa/waste/household.html"]," – although incineration has increased. In 2024 1.86 million tonnes was incinerated, an increase of 239,000 tonnes (14.7%) from 2023. Poorly managed landfill sites can pollute soil and water, release methane and require monitoring long after closure. The ",["1999 EU Landfill Directive","https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/1999/31/oj/eng"],", landfill tax, statutory targets and kerbside collections helped transform the system."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the UK is increasingly burning what it no longer wants to bury. In 2024, 63 energy-from-waste plants burned ",["16.8 million tonnes of residual waste","https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5eabdfbe067c0b62fc7b58b7/t/6800cd36c2408b1f7ad8f645/1744883006223/uk-energy-from-waste-statistics-2024-4812.pdf"],". Since 2024, there are ",["ten incinerators under construction in England and two in Scotland","https://ukwin.org.uk/facts/"],", but none in Wales and Northern Ireland. As people recycle more there’s less need for these, so why are so many being built?"]},{"k":"p","s":["For non-recyclable waste, modern incineration may be preferable to landfill. It reduces waste volume and can ",["generate electricity","https://www.planete-energies.com/en/media/article/incineration-heating-power-refuse"]," or heat. But it is controversial. ",["Incineration is the dirtiest way","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cp3wxgje5pwo"]," the UK generates power. It ",["emits carbon and causes smells","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c1eypqxd928o"]," as well as destroying materials that could otherwise remain in use. It also often causes nearby residents to ",["worry about health risks","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cj45vk7rj0lo"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2024, 82.3% of Scottish household waste classified as “other diversion from landfill” was managed through incineration. ",["Landfilled household waste fell by 37.7%","https://shiny.data.gov.scot/sepa/waste/household.html"],", but the quantity managed through ",["“other diversion” rose by 16.1%","https://shiny.data.gov.scot/sepa/waste/household.html"],". Scotland is therefore managing its residual waste differently, but without achieving an equivalent improvement in waste prevention or recovering or reusing materials."]},{"k":"h","s":["The next waste revolution"]},{"k":"p","s":["The UK’s reduction in how much waste it deposits into landfill was the first waste revolution. The next change must be preventing waste and keeping products and materials in use for longer."]},{"k":"p","s":["Governments should ensure residual waste contracts do not penalise councils for reducing rubbish. They should reward durable, repairable and genuinely recyclable products. Priority should be given to food, flexible plastics, textiles, electrical equipment and complex packaging."]},{"k":"p","s":["Wales shows that sustained recycling progress is also possible. The next waste revolution will begin when conserving materials takes priority over finding another way to destroy them. Those in Scotland who want the country to take an environmental leadership role should take note."]}],"chars":6733}};
